  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Eleven innings and they couldn't close the door until Caballero forced it shut.",
    "what_this_means": "Minnesota had Jos\u00e9 Caballero's sacrifice fly to thank for the 5\u20134 escape, but what lingers is how the Yankees got there. They had chances. Ten runners in scoring position, three converted into runs. That's not a dry night, but it's not enough for a team four and a half back. Rod\u00f3n gave them six innings of control, two runs earned, five strikeouts. The bullpen held clean for five and a third after that. But the offense spent most of this game chasing instead of leading, didn't score until the ninth when they absolutely had to, then spent two more innings fighting for one more run. They got it, but only because Caballero lifted a fly ball in the eleventh. Close games like this feel like wins in the moment. In the division race, they feel like missed opportunities.",
    "what_to_watch": "Arizona sends Eduardo Rodriguez tomorrow night, a 2.62 ERA built on precision this season. Exactly the kind of starter that punishes the Yankees when they fall behind early.",
